WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.081 --> 00:00:02.370
- It's like saying, "Oh
yeah, you can go cheat

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.683
"and I'll just forgive you.

00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:05.120
"Everything will be okay later."

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.707
No, no, that's not how it work.

00:00:06.707 --> 00:00:07.823
I am not Boo Boo the Fool.

00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:10.490
Beyonce is not Boo Boo the Fool.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:16.133
- Living in a world of hookup culture,

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.223
people are constantly
looking for something better

00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:19.154
or what's next.

00:00:19.154 --> 00:00:20.485
Even Jay-Z just dropped
an album addressing

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:22.364
a lot of the rumors we heard on Lemonade.

00:00:22.364 --> 00:00:23.624
So I'm just gonna walk around the office

00:00:23.624 --> 00:00:27.791
and ask, "Could you forgive
someone for cheating on you?"

00:00:30.011 --> 00:00:31.660
- Yes, I have cheated on someone.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.581
- I have not.

00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:34.748
- I don't think they know.

00:00:35.811 --> 00:00:38.076
- I have not been cheated
on, to my knowledge.

00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:39.580
- One time, that I'm aware of.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.747
- I've actually been cheated on

00:00:40.747 --> 00:00:43.047
on two of my serious relationships.

00:00:43.047 --> 00:00:44.504
- I've definitely been cheated on,

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:47.837
and I've definitely cheated to be petty.

00:00:51.252 --> 00:00:53.534
- I can understand why people would cheat.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.482
It doesn't make it right, but sometimes

00:00:55.482 --> 00:00:56.734
things happen in life.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:59.228
- I feel like emotional
cheating's actually a big thing

00:00:59.228 --> 00:01:02.695
even if you're thinking of
someone in a way, that is to me--

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.528
- That's cheating.

00:01:03.528 --> 00:01:04.361
- Almost worse.

00:01:04.361 --> 00:01:07.104
- I feel like if you're a
rapper or a basketball player,

00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:08.549
it's just easier.

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:10.248
- You can't help your attraction.

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:13.032
But, with that being said, your attraction

00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:15.737
should not be open while
you're in a relationship.

00:01:15.737 --> 00:01:17.198
- If you feel like you have to cheat,

00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:21.365
I feel like you should just
get out of that relationship.

00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:26.471
- If I'm married, I'm not
gonna leave my husband

00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:27.882
for cheating.

00:01:27.882 --> 00:01:30.104
If it's something that happened once.

00:01:30.104 --> 00:01:32.007
- Does that mean you get
back together with them

00:01:32.007 --> 00:01:34.782
and forgive them enough to
keep the relationship going?

00:01:34.782 --> 00:01:36.762
Or do you forgive them
enough where it's like

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:38.714
you're kind of okay with
the choices they've made

00:01:38.714 --> 00:01:39.898
as a person?

00:01:39.898 --> 00:01:41.193
- I feel like you forgive somebody

00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:43.581
if you're the family or you
have some sort of history

00:01:43.581 --> 00:01:44.643
or past.

00:01:44.643 --> 00:01:46.772
I think it's tough for people
just to leave that behind.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:50.365
- As a single person with no children,

00:01:50.365 --> 00:01:52.624
for me, cheating is a deal-breaker.

00:01:52.624 --> 00:01:54.940
- I would forgive them
because that's just how I am

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.387
and that's my morals but I would not stay

00:01:57.387 --> 00:01:58.408
in a relationship with them.

00:01:58.408 --> 00:02:00.680
- Obviously, your life is now devoted

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.203
to your kids and your family
but you at the end of the day

00:02:03.203 --> 00:02:04.605
need to be happy.

00:02:04.605 --> 00:02:08.599
- Forgiveness is the way to
move on and grow but it's

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:10.016
really difficult.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.217
(slow urban music)

